from build_audit import *

F=[]
def finding(id,priority,title,evidence,error,correction):F.append(dict(id=id,priority=priority,title=title,evidence=evidence,likely_answer_error=error,correction=correction))
finding('F01','P1','The two current-linked Milan timetables conflict with the current T2S baseline',[
 cite('dd1cf7cb930b','30 June 2025, PDF 13 (printed 9): NTS 19:30; PDF 15 (printed 11): two partial windows'),cite('milan-it-settlement','Italian original, PDF 12 and 15: same stale timetable'),cite('aa3d5a3b94c9','R2026.JUN, Table 37 PDF 160: NTS 20:00; PDF 162: five partial windows'),cite('8719262f5e8b','26 January 2026, Articles 66–67 PDF 48–49: notices and ECB operating documents')],
 'A current-only query can return 19:30 or two partial windows, while the current platform specification gives 20:00 and five. Italian precedence does not resolve this conflict because both Milan languages contain it.',
 'Quarantine the two timetable passages. For T2S baseline questions use R2026.JUN with dated status notices. Obtain current Milan participant cut-offs/notice chain before answering local submission deadlines; do not invalidate the entire settlement manual.')
finding('F02','P1','A normal timetable is insufficient for a dated operational question',[
 cite('t2s-2026-status-events','8 September 2026 updates at 15:30, 18:10 and 18:55'),cite('aa3d5a3b94c9','R2026.JUN PDF 157: day-specific extensions/contingencies')],
 'An answer about 8 September can assert a 16:00 EUR DvP cut-off even though the official notice postponed it to 17:00. Later incident updates affected the end of day.',
 'Add dated ECB operational status events as scoped exceptions. The 15:30 notice moved EUR DvP by 60 minutes; the 18:55 update says the incident was resolved and IFOP closed at 18:39. Store event time, affected business date/currency, superseding update and whether planned or actual; never turn that exception into the permanent calendar.')
finding('F03','P1','The admitted ISIN workbook mixes listing data and a future programme',[
 cite('ac385b0f3106','Introduction B5:B8; Equities I1/K1/L1 and A2/I2/K2/L2; International ETPs alternative columns'), 'Existing curated-manifest.json: default_retrieval=true; no text_path'],
 'It may identify Euronext as the current designated place on 13 September, or establish Milan eligibility for any ISIN. The workbook instead describes selected European Offering instruments, data through 10 September, with designated/alternative places applying from 21 September.',
 'Remove whole-workbook admission. Split column-level dates/scope, preserve all alternative columns and disclaimers, and use a verified ISIN/link register (including relevant MT-X MT23 data) for operational eligibility. Do not silently rename future columns as current.')
finding('F04','P1','Whole-document defaults exceed the recorded review and metadata controls',[
 'curated-manifest.json: 49 documents marked default_retrieval=true; 38 have empty reviewed_pdf_pages (not proof that no prior reading occurred). Twelve legal captures are also admitted.', 'scripts/finalize_library.py: layer-based default selection; no deployed retriever/chunker found',cite('e1354fb2d76a','May 2026, PDF 16–17: service/role scope is narrower than the group brand')],
 'A broad current/reference label can mix CSD operator duties with participant duties, private interfaces with native T2S, specialist forms with operating rules, or four-CSD corporate-events material with Athens.',
 'Replace defaults with approved propositions and parent sections. Require entity, market, service, role, language, release, security/link/currency context and effective period where material. Unknown required values block operational answers. Treat programme material, historical disclosures and generated explanations separately.')
finding('F05','P1','Text extraction can omit the very requirements a query needs',[
 cite('aa3d5a3b94c9','PDF 269, Diagram 55 and footnote 194: matching fields visible in original but missing from text extraction'), 'evidence/aa3d5a3b94c9-p269.png; original extraction contains the diagram caption without its field matrix', 'Catalogue flags 98 PDFs / 250 low-text pages; 14 archives have member inventories but no audited member extraction'],
 'A schema or matching answer can be incomplete despite a text-rich page and successful extraction. Archive containers can conceal relevant XSD/XML; one nominal ZIP is an XLSX package.',
 'Extract tables/diagrams as structured content plus image and page references; validate cell/field counts and footnotes. Keep payment-type conditions and exceptions with fields. Identify MIME by content, unpack archives in a controlled staging area, deduplicate members and validate XSD dependencies before admission. Do not fill omissions from model memory.')
finding('F06','P1','DORA’s English-labelled capture contains French operative text',[
 cite('02022R2554-20221227','Original browser capture and live recapture, Articles 2 and 64: French body under English navigation'),cite('dora-english-oj','English OJ replacement, Articles 2(1)(g) and 64')],
 'Language filters or English exact-quote requests can retrieve French clauses and silently translate them as verbatim English evidence.',
 'Preserve the original French capture and tag the actual body language. Use the fetched English OJ replacement for the reviewed provisions; verify language at body/chunk level. The law itself is not invalidated by a capture-label defect.')
finding('F07','P2','The Athens version alarm is narrower than the existing register suggests',[
 cite('d89c56df8c5a','English PDF 2 and 217, Section XIII Part 9 / footnote 94'),cite('athens-greek-master','Greek PDF 2 and 206; live Greek hub labels it Edition 8'),cite('57a7e76436ca','HCMC official CSD route: connection refused during audit')],
 'Blanket rejection of the master can hide relevant current rules; accepting “Amendment 8” as verified history is also wrong. Both sampled texts identify seven amendments and the seventh’s 8 December 2025 effective date.',
 'Record probable edition-versus-amendment labelling (inference), not an established operative-text conflict. Preserve separate board, approval, Gazette and provision-effective dates. Permit only the checked identity proposition until operational clauses and the independent approval decision are reviewed.')
finding('F08','P2','Oslo’s edition approval qualification remains unresolved',[
 cite('14dc34b8e54e','English VPO NOK cover, effective 2 September 2024 subject to approval'),cite('822d46bb9149','Norwegian cover contains the same reservation'),cite('1ee1619da83d','Regulator infrastructure page: system approval, not the identified rulebook-edition approval')],
 'An answer may assert unconditional binding status for this edition. Conversely, dropping all of Oslo would unnecessarily discard separately reviewed registration rules.',
 'Quarantine unconditional legal-status claims for the VPO NOK edition. Seek the exact Finanstilsynet approval or an authoritative unconditional successor; keep qualified descriptions and other Oslo services separately scoped.')
finding('F09','P2','Future application and release publication need finer states',[
 cite('7244cf50f753','R2026.NOV draft note PDF 1–2: final publication planned 11 September; current hub still draft at audit'),cite('c164d86ada8e','R2026.JUN final cover note'),cite('t2s-2026-status-events','14 June 2026 deployment confirmation'),cite('32025R2075','Articles 1–2: adopted T+1 law applies 11 October 2027'),cite('591deafae0a9','C(2026)4640 final Article 2: 7 December 2026, 1 July 2027 and 11 October 2027 application stages')],
 'The library may treat a missed publication target as proof a final specification exists, promote an undeployed release, call adopted law a draft, or apply all settlement-discipline changes on one date.',
 'Separate adoption, publication, approval, entry into force, application and deployment. June is supported by final documentation plus deployment evidence. November final publication remains unverified. European Offering is still announced for 21 September and Convergence remains a programme on 13 September; reassess dates per service without auto-promotion.')
finding('F10','P2','Known date anomalies should be resolved or retained precisely',[
 cite('cbdf3c1f8b51','Part 2 cover 3 August 2026; PDF 2–3 footers disagree 13/12'),cite('14e2c64da9a0','January 2026 fee book, cover/revision'),cite('cdd34eb011e9','November 2026 fee book, cover/revision'),cite('089b7aaef991','V43: internal January 26 date, February 16 filename, April URL; Chapter 4 delegates calendar/hours')],
 'Publication/filename chronology can select the wrong fee period or create an unsupported effective date. A footer discrepancy can be overstated as a conflicting edition.',
 'Use cover/version/hash and explicit charging periods. January Copenhagen fees are the current candidate; November fees future. Preserve Porto effective date as unknown, and obtain governing notices. Do not invent a 2024 Porto regulation amendment from a similarly numbered circular.')
